{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'defn (init-client|rebind)|attach|cursor|decoder|established|detached' src/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/ws.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"2:  \"The WebSocket decoder for the DaoStream v2 RPC core.\n7:   and it constructs RPC client state from a whole WebSocket `attach!`\n11:   promise, cursor, or scheduler is created or retained; the caller owns all\n20:(def envelope-attachment-key :ws/attachment)\n35:  \"Every deposited event kind this decoder recognizes from the WebSocket\n47:   each establish the attachment.  The offer's host-local `:ws/handle` is a\n49:  {opened-event :dao.stream.apply/established\n50:   accepted-event :dao.stream.apply/established\n51:   closed-event :dao.stream.apply/detached\n63:;; The decoder\n66:(defn decoder\n67:  \"Return the envelope decoder for one attachment identity.\n72:   - an envelope of another attachment (or, on a shared medium, one that\n74:     consumed once by the caller's cursor and is never a response;\n83:     decoder open to additive transport vocabulary;\n88:   `me` may be nil for a private medium, in which case no attachment\n89:   filtering is applied.  The decoder closes over `me` only; reattachment\n90:   must build a fresh decoder through `rebind`.\"\n98:        (and (some? me) (not= me (get envelope envelope-attachment-key)))\n118:  decoder)\n122:;; Client construction from a whole attach! result\n125:(defn- checked-attach\n126:  [attach-result]\n127:  (when-not (and (map? attach-result)\n128:                 (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome attach-result))\n129:                 (contains? attach-result :dao.stream/handle))\n130:    (throw (ex-info \"RPC client requires a successful WebSocket attach! result\"\n131:                    {:ws/attach attach-result})))\n132:  attach-result)\n135:(defn init-client\n136:  \"Construct RPC client state from a whole WebSocket `attach!` result.\n139:   mints one, the attachment identity the response decoder filters on; a\n140:   transport without attachment identity leaves `:me` nil and decoding\n141:   unfiltered.  `reader` and `response-cursor` name the host-composed\n142:   response medium and its already-minted cursor.  No cursor is fabricated\n143:   here.  A failed or contract-violating attach result is a composition\n145:  [attach-result reader response-cursor]\n146:  (let [attach (checked-attach attach-result)\n147:        me (:dao.stream/attachment attach)]\n148:    (rpc/client-state (:dao.stream/handle attach) reader response-cursor\n149:                      {:me me :decode (decoder me)})))\n152:(defn rebind\n153:  \"Reattach a detached WebSocket client to a fresh `attach!` result.\n155:   Only a `/detached` terminal is reconnectable; every other terminal reason\n156:   returns `state` unchanged.  A rebind keeps the response reader, cursor,\n158:   decoder around the new attachment identity -- without that the client\n159:   would keep filtering on the dead attachment and drop everything the new\n161:  [state attach-result]\n162:  (if-not (= :dao.stream.apply/detached (:terminal state))\n164:    (let [attach (checked-attach attach-result)\n165:          me (:dao.stream/attachment attach)]\n166:      (assoc (rpc/rebind state (:dao.stream/handle attach) me)\n167:             :decode (decoder me)))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
