{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '361,610p' collab/architect-dao-jing-v2-plan.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md | nl -ba -v361\"","aggregated_output":"   361\t## Phase J0 — What exists\n   362\t\n   363\tRecorded so the phases start from evidence.\n   364\t\n   365\t- `dao.stream` (protocols, outcome sets, `validate-outcome`), the ring\n   366\t  buffer with `make-attacher`, `dao.stream.apply` (envelope, `serve-once!`),\n   367\t  `dao.stream.rpc` (`client-state`, `request!`, `poll!`, `take-completed`,\n   368\t  `take-diagnostics`, `unsent?`, `rebind`), `dao.stream.rpc.ws`\n   369\t  (`decoder`, `init-client`, `rebind`), `dao.stream.ws` with host\n   370\t  `connect!` seams on clj, cljs and cljd, `dao.stream.serving`, and the\n   371\t  conformance harness. All green per the user on this revision.\n   372\t- `dao.jing` core and `dao.jing.mem` are stream-free.\n   373\t- `test/dao/jing_test.cljc` observer cases (lines 322–561) are the behavioral\n   374\t  evidence for J2; `test/dao/jing/file_test.cljc` for J1;\n   375\t  `test/dao/jing/remote_test.cljc` for J3; `test/dao/stream/rpc_test.cljc`\n   376\t  is the shape precedent for the socket-free J3 tests.\n   377\t\n   378\t## Phase J1 — `dao.jing.file` without a stream\n   379\t\n   380\t- Replace the five `ds/*` sites with a private framed-file section:\n   381\t  `open-frames!` (create parent dirs, open read/write, truncate an incomplete\n   382\t  tail exactly as `dao.stream.log/make-log-stream` does), `append-frame!`\n   383\t  (length prefix + bytes at the current end, then sync), `replay-frames`\n   384\t  (every complete record from offset 0), `close-frames!`. Three host branches,\n   385\t  `:cljd` first.\n   386\t- `put` is unchanged in order: validate, lock, closed check, presence check,\n   387\t  append and sync, then swap the content map, then `:inserted`. `close!` stays\n   388\t  idempotent. Both drop `dao.stream` and `dao.stream.log` from the requires.\n   389\t- Public `records`: `(records path)` returns the decoded, validated\n   390\t  `[address payload]` vector of a file, for tests and diagnostics; it opens,\n   391\t  replays and closes.\n   392\t- **On-disk compatibility test.** A golden byte sequence for one known record\n   393\t  is written to a temp path by hand; `create-content-file` must read it and\n   394\t  `records` must return it. This is what proves the framing did not drift.\n   395\t- Port `file_test`: `handle-shape-test` asserts no `:log` and no `:stream`;\n   396\t  every `count-records` becomes `(count (records path))`; the corrupt-record\n   397\t  and raw-duplicate cases write their raw frames through `append-frame!`.\n   398\t  `observer-convergence-test` moves to J2 (it needs the v2 observer).\n   399\t\n   400\tDeliverable: `dao.jing.file` requires no `dao.stream*` namespace;\n   401\t`file_test` green on clj, cljs (Node) and cljd with `dao.stream` absent from\n   402\tits requires. Consumers (`dao.space.*`, `dao.data.btree_durability_test`) pass\n   403\tunchanged, confirmed by running them rather than by inspection.\n   404\t\n   405\t## Phase J2 — `dao.jing.v2`, the observer\n   406\t\n   407\t`src/cljc/dao/jing/v2.cljc`: `observer-state`, `observe-step!`, `adopt-cursor`,\n   408\tper *Decision 1*. Requires `dao.jing` and `dao.stream` only.\n   409\t\n   410\tTests, `test/dao/jing/v2_test.cljc`, over v2 ring buffers created with\n   411\t`ringbuffer/create!` and cursors minted with `stream/cursor … :dao.stream/oldest`:\n   412\t\n   413\t- every observer case in `jing_test.cljc` lines 322–561, ported: plain-data\n   414\t  state, empty pool blocked, all blocked, hashing and retrieval, equal\n   415\t  payloads from two streams converge, blocked/ended members do not starve\n   416\t  others, all ended, drains then end, fair round-robin, strict interleave,\n   417\t  cursor advances only after successful materialization. Cursor assertions\n   418\t  become successor-equality assertions (`(= (:dao.stream/cursor res) …)`)\n   419\t  never position arithmetic.\n   420\t- **gap**: a capacity-2 ring buffer with three appends; the signal is\n   421\t  `:dao.stream/gap` with `:member 0` and a `:cursor`; the member cursor is\n   422\t  unchanged; the other member still progresses; the gap reports again on the\n   423\t  next turn; after `adopt-cursor` with the recovery cursor the member\n   424\t  materializes the live value.\n   425\t- **defect outcomes**: a reified reader handle scripted to answer\n   426\t  `cursor-mismatch`, `invalid-cursor`, `transport-error` (and, for the\n   427\t  totality test, each outcome in `dao.stream/outcomes-next`); assert the\n   428\t  signal, `:member`, `:result`, unchanged cursor, and that an outcome outside\n   429\t  the declared set throws.\n   430\t- **members round-trip**: `(observer-state (remove-nth (:members st) i))`\n   431\t  keeps the remaining members' cursors.\n   432\t- `observer-convergence-test` from `file_test`, over the J1 file backend.\n   433\t\n   434\tDeliverable: `dao.jing.v2` on clj, cljs (Node) and cljd; `Testing\n   435\tdao.jing.v2-test` confirmed in the Node output; no namespace under\n   436\t`dao.jing.v2*` requires `dao.stream`.\n   437\t\n   438\t## Phase J3 — `dao.jing.v2.remote`\n   439\t\n   440\t**J3a — socket-free, all three hosts.** `src/cljc/dao/jing/v2/remote.cljc`\n   441\tper *Decision 3*. Tests, `test/dao/jing/v2/remote_test.cljc`, mirror\n   442\t`rpc_test.cljc`: request and response media are two ring buffers; the server\n   443\tside is `apply/server-state` + `apply/serve-once!` over `default-handlers`\n   444\ton a `dao.jing.mem` store; the client is `rpc/client-state` over the same\n   445\tmedia, wrapped by `client-state`.\n   446\t\n   447\t- put then get round-trips through `step`; duplicate put completes `:present`;\n   448\t  absent get completes `:found? false`; a stored `nil` and a stored\n   449\t  `{:found? true :value \"hello\"}` round-trip exactly (the envelope-shaped\n   450\t  payload case from v1's `network-presence-envelope-test`).\n   451\t- `request-*` on a non-segment address throws before allocation; a handler\n   452\t  rejecting a hash-mismatched address completes as `:error`.\n   453\t- a scripted writer answering `full` once: `pending-request`, then `busy` on a\n   454\t  second request, then `requested` after a step; exactly one id allocated.\n   455\t- gap on the response medium and `/detached` complete every outstanding\n   456\t  request as `:lost`; malformed responses complete as `:error` with the\n   457\t  malformed-response code and never as `:found?`.\n   458\t- completions publish exactly once; `:completed` empty after `step`.\n   459\t- `default-handlers` on a handle without `:put-content-fn` throws at\n   460\t  construction.\n   461\t\n   462\t**J3b — over `dao.stream.ws`, same process, all three hosts.** A serving\n   463\tcomposition assembled in the test from `dao.stream.serving` and the host\n   464\t`connect!`/`bind!` seams, exactly as `test/dao/stream/ws_test.cljc` and\n   465\t`serving_test.cljc` do; the served stream is a capacity-1 identity anchor as\n   466\tthe REPL's D3 settled. The client mints its `:dao.stream/newest` cursor on\n   467\tits traffic medium *before* `attach!`, builds the RPC state with\n   468\t`rpc.ws/init-client` from the whole `attach!` result, and wraps it with\n   469\t`client-state`. Prove: put and get round-trip over the wire; two clients see\n   470\teach other's writes; the file backend survives a stop, restart and reattach\n   471\t(v1's `network-file-restart-test`); killing the connection completes the\n   472\toutstanding request as `:lost` with `/detached` and `rebind` after a fresh\n   473\t`attach!` resumes with the same cursor; a descriptor naming a path nothing\n   474\tserves completes as `:lost` with `/not-found`.\n   475\t\n   476\tDeliverable: J3a green on clj, cljs (Node) and cljd; J3b green on clj and cljs\n   477\t(Node), and on cljd through the cljd ws lane. The cljd test regenerates\n   478\t`test/cljd-out/`; one process owns it at a time.\n   479\t\n   480\t## Phase J4 — Design prose\n   481\t\n   482\t`dao.jing.md`, exactly the sections *Decision 1* names, plus: *Implemented\n   483\tsurface* describes `dao.jing.file` as \"a content-addressed store backed by a\n   484\tprivate framed append-only file\" and `dao.jing.v2.remote` as handlers plus a\n   485\tclient state machine the composition drives, and states that `jing/materialize!`\n   486\tand `jing/get` are local operations that do not apply to a remote store. The\n   487\t*Reads* paragraph that says a reader \"may access the target … through a remote\n   488\ttransport (`dao.jing.remote`, `dao.jing.dht`)\" gains \"as a request whose answer\n   489\tarrives as a completion\". `dao.jing.dht.md` is not edited.\n   490\t\n   491\tThe v1 observer's docstrings in `dao.jing` are not edited; they go with it.\n   492\t\n   493\t## Phase J5 — Deletion and the naming decision\n   494\t\n   495\tGated on `dao.space`'s migration: it is the last consumer of the v1 observer\n   496\t(through its tests) and of v1 `dao.jing.remote` (through `dao.jing.coordinate`\n   497\tand its tests). When that gate opens:\n   498\t\n   499\t- delete `observer-state` and `observe-step!` from `dao.jing` and its\n   500\t  `dao.stream` require; delete the observer section of `jing_test.cljc`;\n   501\t- delete `src/cljc/dao/jing/remote.cljc` and `test/dao/jing/remote_test.cljc`;\n   502\t  `dao.jing.coordinate`'s `:dao.jing/remote` branch is deleted or re-pointed\n   503\t  under `dao.space`'s plan, not here;\n   504\t- take **one explicit decision**, mirroring the stream plan's end condition.\n   505\t  The recommendation is to **fold back**: move the v2 observer into `dao.jing`\n   506\t  and rename `dao.jing.v2.remote` to `dao.jing.remote`, in the same change as\n   507\t  `dao.stream`'s rename if that is the decision there. DaoJing's namespace\n   508\t  names appear on no wire and in no coordinate — coordinate types are\n   509\t  keywords like `:dao.jing/file`, unaffected — so only requires change. An\n   510\t  undecided coexistence is a defect of the migration, not a steady state.\n   511\t\n   512\t## Host matrix\n   513\t\n   514\t| phase | clj | cljs (Node) | cljd | notes                                                                                     |\n   515\t| ----- | --- | ----------- | ---- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n   516\t| J1    | ✓   | ✓           | ✓    | three host branches in `dao.jing.file`, `:cljd` first; Node uses synchronous `fs`         |\n   517\t| J2    | ✓   | ✓           | ✓    | pure `.cljc`, no host branch                                                              |\n   518\t| J3a   | ✓   | ✓           | ✓    | pure `.cljc`, no host branch                                                              |\n   519\t| J3b   | ✓   | ✓           | ✓    | composition uses the per-host `connect!` seam; cljd through the cljd ws lane              |\n   520\t| J4    | —   | —           | —    | prose                                                                                     |\n   521\t| J5    | ✓   | ✓           | ✓    | deletions; confirm every `dao.jing*` test namespace still appears in each host's output   |\n   522\t\n   523\tPer the standing rule, confirm `Testing dao.jing.v2-test` and `Testing\n   524\tdao.jing.v2.remote-test` appear in the Node output rather than assuming\n   525\tdiscovery.\n   526\t\n   527\t## Invariants, checked\n   528\t\n   529\t- **No hidden global state.** `dao.jing.v2` holds no atom. `dao.jing.file`'s\n   530\t  state atom and lock are per-handle and explicit, as `dao.jing.mem`'s are.\n   531\t  No `defopen`, no dispatch table, no `defonce`.\n   532\t- **No implicit control flow.** `observe-step!` and `step` return; the\n   533\t  composition calls again. Nothing self-schedules.\n   534\t- **No callbacks.** None in any new public surface. The ws adapter map is the\n   535\t  transport's, confined to J3b's composition.\n   536\t- **No shared mutable state.** A content handle is owned by whoever created\n   537\t  it; the RPC state is a value threaded by one driver.\n   538\t- **Interpretation and execution stay separate.** The observer interprets the\n   539\t  pool; the backend executes the write; the remote client interprets\n   540\t  completions; the serving composition executes the socket.\n   541\t- **No assumed graphs.** Nothing here relates content addresses to each other.\n   542\t\n   543\t## Boundary of this plan\n   544\t\n   545\t**Untouched:** `dao.jing` core and its v1 observer until J5; `dao.jing.mem`;\n   546\t`dao.jing.remote` until J5; `dao.jing.coordinate`; `dao.jing.dht`,\n   547\t`dao.jing.dht.kad`, `dao.jing.dht.node`; every `dao.space*` and\n   548\t`dao.data.btree*` namespace and test; `dao.stream` v1 in every form.\n   549\t\n   550\t**Architectural decisions**, made here: the durable log is not a stream\n   551\t(Decision 2); remote content is a driven state machine, not a handle\n   552\t(Decision 3); the observer's cursor and non-progress discipline (Decision 1);\n   553\tparallel-versus-in-place by whether a v1 consumer remains (Decision 4).\n   554\t\n   555\t**Implementation gaps**, left open knowingly: the v2 remote client has no\n   556\tcoordinate and cannot be reached from `dao.jing.coordinate/open!`; the\n   557\tserving side exists only as test compositions.\n   558\t\n   559\t**Intentionally deferred**, each to a named home:\n   560\t\n   561\t- `dao.jing.dht` and `dao.jing.dht.node` — UDP transport, deferred by the\n   562\t  stream plan; `dht.cljc` itself requires no `dao.stream`, and `node.cljc`'s\n   563\t  `dao.stream.transit` require goes with the UDP transport's own migration.\n   564\t- `dao.space`'s own migration: `publish-index!`'s v1 `ds/append!` into the\n   565\t  intake pool, `snapshot-datoms`' `{:position 0}` walk, the published-index\n   566\t  `defopen`, `DaoStreamLog`'s writer face, and switching its tests to\n   567\t  `dao.jing.v2`.\n   568\t- The `:dao.jing/remote` coordinate under v2 and async B-tree hydration\n   569\t  (`dao.data.btree.md` §5.4) — `dao.space`'s query-side plan; this client is\n   570\t  the \"async DaoJing backend\" that section waits for.\n   571\t- A content-serving endpoint as production infrastructure — the composition\n   572\t  that starts, serves and stops a content server belongs to whatever product\n   573\t  surface needs it, as the REPL's R4 did for the REPL.\n   574\t- Canonical encoding; durable observer checkpoints and a long-running runner;\n   575\t  explicit materialization acknowledgement; garbage collection — the four\n   576\t  open items of `dao.jing.md`, unchanged by this plan. Checkpoints gain only\n   577\t  the shape constraint that the persisted value is the transport's own cursor,\n   578\t  whose serializability the contract leaves TBD.\n   579\t- A v2 file or append-log transport — until a consumer needs cursors over a\n   580\t  durable file.\n   581\t\n   582\t## End condition\n   583\t\n   584\tComplete when all of the following hold on clj, cljs (Node) and cljd:\n   585\t\n   586\t- `dao.jing.file` requires no `dao.stream*` namespace, reads every content\n   587\t  file v1 wrote, and its suite runs with no stream fixture.\n   588\t- `dao.jing.v2` observes v2 reader handles with stream-minted cursors, is\n   589\t  total over `dao.stream/outcomes-next` by a declaration-driven test,\n   590\t  retains only successors and adopted cursors, and requires only `dao.jing`\n   591\t  and `dao.stream`.\n   592\t- `dao.jing.v2.remote` round-trips put and get through `dao.stream.apply`\n   593\t  and `dao.stream.rpc` over ring buffers on all three hosts and over\n   594\t  `dao.stream.ws` on each, completing lost requests as data.\n   595\t- `dao.jing.md` describes the v2 observer, the stream-free file backend and\n   596\t  the driven remote client.\n   597\t- No namespace under `dao.jing.v2*` requires `dao.stream` or\n   598\t  `dao.stream.rpc.*`.\n   599\t- Once `dao.space` has migrated: the v1 observer and v1 `dao.jing.remote` are\n   600\t  deleted, and the naming decision has been taken explicitly.\n   601\t\n   602\t---\n   603\t\n   604\t## Decisions most likely to be contested in review\n   605\t\n   606\t1. **Decision 2 (b)** — removing the stream from the file backend rather than\n   607\t   building a v2 log transport. The counter-argument is Axiom 1 read\n   608\t   literally; the answer is that the log has one reader who is its only\n   609\t   writer, and that `dao.jing.mem` already sets the precedent.\n   610\t2. **Keeping the on-disk framing** byte-for-byte instead of taking the chance\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
